      {[
        {
          id: "faq1",
          q: "Should I post from my personal profile or my company page?",
          a: "Your personal profile should be the primary channel. Independent analyses of LinkedIn's distribution consistently show personal profiles reaching significantly more people per post than company pages — estimates range from roughly 2x to 5x depending on the study — because the algorithm is built around individual professional relationships, not brand accounts. Company pages still matter for credibility and SEO, but they shouldn't carry your growth strategy alone."
        },
        {
          id: "faq2",
          q: "How often should a founder post on LinkedIn?",
          a: "Most founders see meaningful engagement growth posting 3–5 times per week, provided the content stays specific to their actual expertise rather than generic advice. Consistency compounds — LinkedIn's distribution rewards accounts with a steady posting history over sporadic high-effort posts."
