        {
          id: "faq3",
          q: "Why do carousels outperform text posts?",
          a: "Carousels currently produce the highest average engagement of any LinkedIn format — around 6.6% versus lower rates for standard text posts. The swipe interaction itself drives additional engagement signals (time spent, multiple interactions per post) that the algorithm reads as strong content."
        },
        {
          id: "faq4",
          q: "Does LinkedIn outreach actually work, or does it feel like spam?",
          a: "It depends entirely on sequencing. Outreach sent cold, with no prior content exposure, performs far worse than outreach sent to people who've already seen and engaged with your posts — in one B2B study, 91% of buyers said they'd respond to outreach from someone whose content they already followed. That's why outreach should run alongside a content strategy, not replace one."
        },
        {
          id: "faq5",
          q: "How long does it take to see results from LinkedIn growth efforts?",
          a: "Engagement and profile-view growth typically becomes visible within the first several weeks of consistent, voice-driven posting. Inbound messages and booked calls usually take longer to build — often two to three months — since they depend on accumulated content history and audience trust, not a single viral post."
        },
        {
          id: "faq6",
          q: "Is LinkedIn worth prioritizing if my customers aren't there?",
          a: "Often yes, even for consumer-facing founders — because LinkedIn's audience skews heavily toward people who influence business decisions: partnerships, hiring, fundraising, and supplier relationships, not just direct sales. A founder building credibility on LinkedIn is usually building it with the people who fund, staff, or partner with the business, not just the end customer."
        },
        {
          id: "faq7",
          q: "What's the difference between a LinkedIn ghostwriter and a LinkedIn management agency?",
          a: "A ghostwriter typically handles writing only. A management agency — like UnitScalers — combines writing, design, outreach, and reporting into one system, so growth doesn't stall if one piece runs dry. It also allows outreach and content to be sequenced together, which is where most of the compounding effect comes from."
        }
      ].map(({ id, q, a }) => (
